  Status: author draft; independent mathematical and source-correspondence
  review pending. Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The prose is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-public-service.tex>.
  It follows the public selected-run path that supplies the per-period
  service receipt used by <verbatim|tentF> and the finite-volume moment
  bound. It proves the finite field assembly from same-history receipts. It
  does not claim to rederive the upstream bought run, tariff, spring, or all
  nonlinear coupon inequalities.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Source
  declarations and files>>|<cell|<strong|Notes>>>|<row|<cell|The selected run
  carries one trail and a purchased same-history
  record>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run>;
  <verbatim|Run.ramp>; <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.again>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Run.ramp> obtains
  the purchased alloy/campaign and calls <verbatim|Bandage.squad> once for
  its selected trail, thresholds, transfer stories, doors, Makes, climbing
  doors, and Freight records. <verbatim|Run.again> calls
  <verbatim|Forge.ahead> using this same purchased tuple, then stores its
  <verbatim|Ties> output and weak specifications.>>|<row|<cell|The
  funded-history producer returns Scrim/Geyser on the same selected
  object>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.ahead>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Unlatched>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Forge.lean>,
  <verbatim|Unlatch.lean>>|<cell|The actual <verbatim|Ahead> field is the
  <verbatim|Unlatched> record. The output of <verbatim|Forge.ahead> includes
  <verbatim|Scrim>, whose <verbatim|costs> field is <verbatim|Geyser>,
  together with tabs, Fridge, portfolios, and purchases. In <verbatim|ahead>,
  the local completion/reception proof is unpacked and assembled into
  same-run aroma and orderwise weak completion; the Scrim field is passed
  unchanged. This is the source boundary for the paid Geyser
  receipt.>>|<row|<cell|Geyser to Ponds conversion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Geyser.pond>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Campaign.ponds>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Pond.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Shroud/Pool.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Geyser.pond>
  copies room, bank, Brine, monotonicity, height, and terminal-music clauses
  into <verbatim|Ponds>, extending initial Brine to the requested reference
  by reindexing. The public <verbatim|Campaign.ponds> construction makes the
  retention clause at each scale from <verbatim|glassDoor>, the selected
  tariff and field exponents; it attaches room/bank budgets,
  <verbatim|evaporates> for Brine, monotonicity, and the gradewise
  height/Freight fields from the selected purchase.>>|<row|<cell|Retention
  and local doors>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.glassDoor>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Stove.escape>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Shroud/WAx.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Stove.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|glassDoor>
  converts the same local realization and tariff into the finite Volant
  ticket and Duty record, using the two endpoint support-exponent lower
  bounds. <verbatim|Stove.escape> supplies Moonlit history from the selected
  nest, Minty conditions, high exponents, and climbing doors. The monograph
  treats those selected inputs as records from the funded package, then
  explains their exact use in the retention field.>>|<row|<cell|Ponds fields
  are consumed by the moment producer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ponds.past>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occursT>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tentF>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Pond.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Dusk/Placed.lean>,
  <verbatim|Tackle.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Ponds.past> combines the gradewise
  Freightage, Fiesta, Cherry, Banks, Brine, and geometry inputs to produce
  the labelwise Nectar service. <verbatim|occursT> calls
  <verbatim|Ponds.past>, obtains servedness using <verbatim|Frost.upper>,
  uses <verbatim|punctual> for weighted coefficient/activity response, and
  applies <verbatim|vista> for finite backward moment transfer.
  <verbatim|tentF> gets migration, occupancy, and Drake data from the
  opened-copy construction and calls <verbatim|occursT>.>>|<row|<cell|Full
  public root-test package>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Campaign.ridgeT>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.oboes>; <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.puddingR>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Dusk/Cargo.lean>, <verbatim|Graff.lean>,
  <verbatim|Mauve.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|ridgeT> constructs
  <verbatim|Mauve.costs> by invoking <verbatim|Campaign.ponds> for every
  period/reference/volume; its other fields are the selected late thresholds,
  <verbatim|Scrim> rates, Fridge, and mark portfolios. <verbatim|oboes> uses
  these costs and the selected schedule to produce the uniform root-test
  bound (<verbatim|Wcmain>). <verbatim|puddingR> then converts that bound and
  the same selected root receipts into a representative label/root-error
  statement.>>>>>

  <section|Explicit upstream boundary><label|explicit-upstream-boundary>

  The purchased <verbatim|Ahead>/<verbatim|Unlatched> record is the actual
  source of the <verbatim|Scrim>/<verbatim|Geyser> data used by this route.
  Its input includes the selected alloy purchase, transition tariff, delayed
  scale choices, same-trail Makes, climbing doors, and Freight records. The
  finite record assembly above does not prove those purchases or the analytic
  ticket estimates in isolation. The separate finite response,
  local-transfer, geometry, and birth-receipt units detail their
  corresponding downstream uses and exact hypotheses. Further derivation of
  any upstream <verbatim|Unlatched> field belongs to the selected-run
  producer path, not to an unselected auxiliary construction.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected only the selected run, same-history producer, and
    immediate Ponds/moment consumers named above; no Lean files were changed
    and no Lean build was run.

    <item>No literature citation is applicable to this finite
    project-specific packaging step.

    <item>The combined temporary wrapper <verbatim|/tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>
    compiled with <verbatim|latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode
    -halt-on-error -outdir=/tmp/ym-centered-fragment-build
    /tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>, producing 38 pages. Pages 37\U38,
    containing this service and local-price argument, were rendered and
    inspected. Eleven unresolved references come from omitted OPE, lattice
    rate/step, and column-subpower units; the only overfull box is in the
    separate lattice chapter.

    <item>The blueprint checker remains subject to the shared parent-owned
    <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> record, which is absent in
    this worktree.
  </itemize-minus>

